{
  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "The best configuration found is config_003 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc 0.7250), and all four aggregation/fusion variants with this encoder pair have been tested. No remaining untested config uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, so beating 0.7250 is very unlikely. The closest untested configuration to the winning pattern is config_043 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted), which keeps the best image encoder, aggregation, and fusion while substituting a simpler RNA encoder. This tests whether the transformer+weighted advantage is robust to RNA encoder choice or is specific to scvi_n200's learned representations. Given this is the final experiment and the best accuracy is already secured, the priority shifts to minimizing cost while extracting useful design-space information. pca_n2000 is a linear method with negligible training overhead, and imagenet_vit_l + transformer is moderate, so expected cost is ~2–3 GPU hours (low relative to the 3.6–4.8 GPU hours of the top scvi_n200 configs). This is the best use of the last slot: it confirms the encoder hierarchy (scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000) at low cost rather than spending 4+ GPU hours on a resnet50 variant that is already known to be inferior to imagenet_vit_l."
}

